.Dd $Mdocdate$
.Dt OSSL_MTC_CA_LOAD_LANDMARKS 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_load_landmarks ,
.Nm OSSL_MTC_CA_add_subtree_hash
.Nd trusted subtrees of a Merkle Tree Certificate authority's logs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Lb libcrypto
.In openssl/mtc.h
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_load_landmarks
.Fa "OSSL_MTC_CA *ca"
.Fa "uint64_t log_number"
.Fa "BIO *in"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_MTC_CA_add_subtree_hash
.Fa "OSSL_MTC_CA *ca"
.Fa "uint64_t log_number"
.Fa "uint64_t start"
.Fa "uint64_t end"
.Fa "const uint8_t *hash"
.Fa "size_t hash_len"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A Merkle Tree Certificate authority publishes, for each of its issuance
logs, a description of the log's active landmarks.
A relying party loads that description to learn which subtrees of the
log are active, then records the hash of each subtree it has verified
through the log's cosigners.
A certificate issued relative to a landmark is accepted only against a
subtree whose hash has been recorded.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_load_landmarks
reads from
.Fa in
a landmark description for log
.Fa log_number
of
.Fa ca
in the format of section 6.4.3 of the Merkle Tree Certificates
specification:
a line holding the number of the newest landmark and the number of
active landmarks, separated by a space,
followed by one line per active landmark and one more,
each holding a tree size, newest first and strictly decreasing.
Every line ends in a newline character and nothing may follow the last.
The log's set of active subtrees is replaced by the subtrees covering the
active landmarks.
A subtree that remains active keeps a hash already recorded for it.
On failure the CA is unchanged.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_MTC_CA_add_subtree_hash
records the
.Fa hash_len
bytes at
.Fa hash
as the hash of the active subtree of log
.Fa log_number
covering the leaves from
.Fa start
inclusive to
.Fa end
exclusive.
.Fa hash_len
must be the output size of the CA's hash algorithm.
Recording the same hash again succeeds; a different hash for a subtree
that already has one is rejected, as is a subtree that is not active.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
These functions return 1 on success or 0 on failure.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr BIO_new 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_MTC_CA_new 3
.Sh STANDARDS
.Rs
